#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# throw_exception

#% text
# `throw_exception(exc)` throws the exception `exc`, tagged by its type, to the nearest `catch_exception` that takes its type.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is `throw(exc, type)`: the value of the call is a failure that propagates through the surrounding computation until it is caught.

#% item
# Without a catching `catch_exception` the failure is the result of the whole evaluation, `failure(thrown, exc, type)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
catch_exception(1 + throw_exception(exception(data_error, assoc(data -> 42))), data_error)
#% output
#= exception(data_error, assoc(data -> 42))

#% text
# Uncaught:

#% cell
throw_exception(exception(data_error))
#% output
#! failure(thrown, exception(data_error, assoc()), data_error)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `catch_exception`, `exception`, `throw`
